# One command, one screen change.
#
# **The command is the `when` and the screen is state.** `create new game` navigates to the planet
# size selector - Sean's design, 2026-10-07 - so the test is that `{screen name:...}` moved and the
# configure screen's own contents are what it shows.
#
# **`configure` offers a selector and two buttons**, which is where a screen's contents stop being
# all one kind: `start` and `back` are action buttons and the selector is a component. **This states
# the selector as one row per size**, which is a choice and is recorded as one.

{test name:create-new-game-goes-to-the-configure-screen}

{given}
{screen name:menu}
{save} -> 0

{when}
{create-new-game}

{then}
{screen name:configure}
{size name:small chosen:0} -> 1
{size name:large chosen:0} -> 1
{item of:configure name:start active:0} -> 1
{item of:configure name:back active:1} -> 1
{attention of:back}
